WEBVTT

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.500
Finally sacked the place, eh?

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:29.160
Has it been a month 
since the Battle of Grad?

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.010
They held out longer than expected.

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:35.490
First the border town of Grad, now Lorgeth.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:37.860
We've secured the strategic 
points in the north.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:40.580
But they've probably used the time

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.870
to fortify their capital 
with forces from all over.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:47.980
We'll need to proceed carefully, then.

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:52.400
Have to wonder how long this 
damned war will go on...

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:56.270
I'll fight for as long as it takes.

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:01.380
<i>What the hell is she smiling about?</i>

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:19.130
The Price of Smiles

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:19.130
<i>The Price of Smiles</i>

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:39.430
<b><i>The Smiling Soldier</i></b>

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:42.640
Hey, Stella.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:46.710
Do you know what our commander's doing here?

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:48.180
He was transferred here, wasn't he?

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.830
Well, I know <i>that</i>.

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:52.270
But what I meant is—

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:54.770
The rumor that he ignored 
an order from above, right?

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:57.650
No one's talking to you, Huey!

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:00.150
It's an entirely baseless rumor.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:03.540
Even before the war, our commander

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:06.670
was assigned missions: 
VIP escorts, stamping out terrorists...

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:09.410
He always carried out his 
orders to the letter.

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:12.750
All the more reason for the rumors, I'd say.

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:16.620
How'd a guy like him end up leading 
a squad like ours, y'know?

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:18.460
What do you mean, "a squad like ours"?

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:22.760
Warrant Officer Break, don't you 
have any pride in our squad?

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:25.500
Don't forget, Pierce.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.890
The guy's been a real creep from the start.

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:30.890
Always looking down his nose 
at us one way or another...

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:35.400
Like "I'm way too classy to 
share a tent with you lot"?

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:37.400
That's it! That's exactly how he—

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:41.790
The <i>point</i> is, he's been 
assigned to us for a month,

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:44.490
but we still don't know anything about him.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:47.910
I don't like putting my life in 
the hands of someone like that.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:51.350
You feel that way, too, Petty Officer Lily?

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:53.410
What do you think, Stella?

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:54.920
I don't know.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:58.900
On the eastern edge of the State of Caldath

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:01.580
lies a city called Azaria.

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:04.330
It's said to be a quiet place
 ruled by a local lord.

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:06.550
What's its significance?

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:10.320
According to prisoners we took 
at the Battle of Lorgeth,

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:14.690
there's a chance some supplies have 
been left at the local forces' base.

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:18.230
But we can't afford to lose 
forces in another battle

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:20.970
with nothing to show for it in the end.

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:23.200
You want us to perform recon?

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:27.320
It seems the local lord took 
the bulk of his army to guard Hariant.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:30.430
Only a small local force should be present.

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:33.020
Infiltration shouldn't be difficult.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:35.850
That ends the briefing.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:38.660
We'll depart at 0800 tomorrow.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:40.090
Any questions?

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:42.810
Sounds like a relaxing change of pace to me.

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:44.600
Petty Officer Huey.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:48.050
People who say things like that 
tend to be the first to die.

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.100
Scary.

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:51.810
Pierce and Break, once we arrive,

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:54.380
you'll stand by in theurgears
 on the city's east side.

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:55.300
Yes, sir.

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:55.730
Yes, sir.

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:58.360
The rest of us will investigate the city.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.230
Yes, sir.

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:00.230
Yes, sir.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:01.590
Yes, sir.

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:20.750
After we scouting the location, 
we'll rendezvous here at 2000 hours.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:29.780
For being out in the boonies, 
they've got some pretty nice stuff...

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:33.400
I knew they were at a different 
phase of industrialization,

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:36.890
but it's still a shock to see it up close.

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:40.770
Hey, that one would look great on Stella!

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:44.280
So would that one!

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:48.800
And Soleil wants to keep all 
of this to themselves...

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:52.340
Yuki Soleil?

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:55.040
She really is still a child, isn't she?

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:59.820
If you had to kill that princess...

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:01.290
what would you do?

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:05.170
I'd kill her if I was ordered to, of course.

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:14.280
Appreciate the patronage.

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:15.430
Thanks for coming by.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:22.940
So this is their food storehouse?

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:26.040
I certainly hope they've 
left some behind, but...

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:36.420
As I thought, it's all 
been taken out, hasn't it?

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:39.960
Given the state of the conflict, 
it's not surprising.

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:42.960
Are we struggling for other resources, too?

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:51.720
Show yourself.

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:00.050
What are you doing?

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:01.850
Mauli!

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.460
Alan!

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:05.570
I told you not to come in here!

00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:07.310
I'm sorry.

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:09.250
Put it back.

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:17.960
I'm sorry. We'll be going now.

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:19.870
Wait. Who are you?

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:24.170
We live in the administrative building.

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:25.310
Administrative building?

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:27.380
Since no one's using it at the moment.

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:29.510
And you're living there, long-term?

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:34.710
Hey. You guys work for a laundry, right?

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:35.970
What are you doing here?

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:40.600
A friend of ours works in this storehouse.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:43.350
We thought we'd drop in on him 
while we were on the job...

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:46.870
They took all the food out of here yesterday.

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:49.990
Your friend probably went with them.

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:51.500
Most likely.

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:53.770
We'd better go.

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:55.870
We'll get an earful from 
the Order if they see us.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:57.240
The Order?

00:07:58.550 --> 00:07:59.940
Let's go, Mauli.

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:01.320
Wait a minute.

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:04.500
The Order would be less likely 
to see you in a truck, right?

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:13.540
One, two... three!

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:16.260
Run!

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:24.020
Mauli!

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:25.770
Alan!

00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:27.410
Where have you been?

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:28.870
The food storehouse.

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:31.700
Who are they?

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:33.070
They're the laundry guys.

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:34.750
They gave us a ride in their truck!

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:35.650
No fair!

00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:37.710
How'd things go at the storehouse? 
You find any food?

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:39.580
I found some canned fruit, but...

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:41.290
You know we couldn't take it with us.

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:44.830
But the old guy has it.

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:47.410
Look! Look!

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:52.550
I'm a sucker for sweets, that's all.

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:53.870
You...

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:56.240
Besides, it's close to its expiration date.

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:58.440
It would just spoil if we left it there.

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:00.980
Better to share it among us, I think.

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:01.960
How about you?

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:10.440
Let the children have some, please.

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:12.940
All right!

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:15.570
C'mon, Lana! Have some with us!

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:22.640
Here!

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:25.330
So good!

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:25.240
Calm down!

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:36.310
You're not going to join them?

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:40.350
I'm Stella.

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:43.200
Lana.

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:47.250
That's a cute doll.

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:50.110
Papa and Mama bought her for me.

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:52.980
She's important to you, then?

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:54.090
Yeah.

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:57.240
They both died in the war.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:01.740
Everyone else is the same as me.

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:05.500
They said they brought us 
here because it was safe.

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:12.580
Did you like that?

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:13.620
Yeah!

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:18.160
Speaking of which, that Order 
you mentioned before...

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:20.060
Would that be Hariant's chivalric order?

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:21.010
Yeah.

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:23.610
I've never met them before.

00:10:23.610 --> 00:10:24.790
Have they been here a while?

00:10:25.530 --> 00:10:26.520
They have, right?

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:27.290
Yeah.

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:28.780
In that building.

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:29.640
Yeah.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:35.330
I see.

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:36.610
Well, seeing as they're valued clients,

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.900
we ought to stop by and pay our respects.

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:41.780
Shall we?

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:03.300
Go! Go!

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:04.810
Hey, Lana.

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:07.060
Not fair!

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:08.640
Hey, let me try!

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:10.680
If...

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:16.570
If you feel like there's nowhere in 
the world where you belong, don't worry.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:20.070
You'll find your place someday.

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:22.700
Really?

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:25.940
I was the same as you.

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:29.200
Did you find a place?

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:31.140
Yes.

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:39.970
Here.

00:11:42.370 --> 00:11:43.370
Thank you.

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:47.150
Lieutenant.

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:50.230
I can't get in touch with 
Special Ensign Owens.

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:53.800
He's running an infiltration right now.

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:56.470
He'll be out of touch until 
his scheduled contact time.

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:58.850
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:11:58.850 --> 00:12:03.490
He learned that the Order are here 
in the base, so he's investigating.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:04.900
<i>The Order?</i>

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:05.780
Yes.

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:08.490
<i>We've just received word from 
the Hariant scouting party</i>

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:12.050
<i>that the Soleil Army is heading for Azaria.</i>

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:13.750
<i>A battalion, it seems.</i>

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:15.880
A battalion? Coming here?

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:16.940
<i>Yes.</i>

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:20.880
<i>It might be related to whatever 
the Order is doing there.</i>

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:33.550
This is...

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:39.650
A food plant powered by the new chrars?

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:43.220
Just one of 'em is enough 
to run a plant of that size?

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:45.530
Talk about an exponential upgrade...

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:51.290
I suspect the Royal Army is coming to 
carry these provisions to the front lines.

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:53.790
<i>Chief of Staff Fleet.</i>

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:55.170
<i>What do you recommend?</i>

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:59.910
<i>At the moment, we can't spare 
the forces to engage the battalion.</i>

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:02.920
<i>Special Ensign Gail Owens.</i>

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:06.630
<i>Can you obtain the new chrars 
and destroy the plant</i>

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:08.680
<i>before the Royal Army arrives?</i>

00:13:10.400 --> 00:13:11.490
<i>What's the matter?</i>

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:12.870
I can.

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:15.690
But it might result in civilian casualties.

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:17.150
<i>A necessary evil.</i>

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:19.960
<i>If the food produced by that new chrars</i>

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:22.080
<i>were to be distributed across Soleil,</i>

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:24.320
<i>the tide of battle would 
swiftly turn against us.</i>

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:30.250
<i>The longer the fighting drags on, 
the more our people will suffer.</i>

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:32.700
Understood.

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:38.330
<i>Just in case, we're sending two 
twelve-gun batteries your way.</i>

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:40.310
You mean...

00:13:40.310 --> 00:13:44.230
<i>If you fail, we'll bombard the plant 
from long range and destroy it</i>

00:13:44.230 --> 00:13:47.090
<i>before the battalion arrives.</i>

00:13:48.190 --> 00:13:51.850
<i>We expect the enemy battalion to 
arrive in roughly three hours.</i>

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:57.330
<i>Thus, the battery will open fire 
two hours from now, at 2300 hours.</i>

00:13:58.520 --> 00:13:59.450
Roger that.

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:02.730
Two hours? Is she insane?

00:14:03.050 --> 00:14:05.540
I'll fill you in on the plan on the way.

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:07.780
Though it's not exactly our speed...

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:31.140
Those children are all war orphans, she said.

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:32.870
I bet.

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:38.980
We're starting the infiltration now.

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:40.400
Follow the plan.

00:14:40.680 --> 00:14:41.680
<i>Roger that.</i>

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:43.020
<i>Just leave it to us.</i>

00:14:44.210 --> 00:14:46.410
I'll be parting ways with you for now.

00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:47.750
Huh?

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:49.030
What are you talking about?

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:51.100
You guys just follow the plan.

00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:54.410
Get that new chrars and blow up the plant.

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:55.690
And you, Commander?

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:56.810
I've got an errand to run.

00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:58.290
You're in charge until I get back.

00:14:59.090 --> 00:15:00.780
You're crazy, old man!

00:15:00.780 --> 00:15:02.040
I completely agree!

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:04.400
Understood.

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:06.170
We'll carry out the mission ourselves.

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:07.370
Oh, boy...

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:08.300
Stella...

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:09.160
Let's go.

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:11.050
Freaking hell.

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:13.170
Who gave that guy command?

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:33.320
The chrars is still running, 
so we need to shut it down first.

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:39.330
We'll need to use both this terminal 
and the one on the installation itself.

00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:41.710
Understood. I'll handle that.

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:43.210
I'm counting on you.

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:15.240
I've got one straight ahead.

00:16:15.710 --> 00:16:16.620
Same.

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:19.780
Three, two, one...

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:33.980
Y-You...

00:16:33.980 --> 00:16:36.010
Round the others up quickly.

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:50.030
Delicious!

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:55.780
<i>Lily.</i>

00:16:55.940 --> 00:16:57.250
I've got it shut down here.

00:16:58.290 --> 00:16:59.840
Shut down here, too.

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:01.930
<i>Stella, behind you!</i>

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:04.040
You! What are you doing?

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:07.450
Intruders!

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:14.550
Perfect timing!

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:22.810
C'mon! Hurry up, everyone!

00:17:23.150 --> 00:17:24.180
Stay where you are!

00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:28.770
Let's go.

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:30.400
Wait! Don't go with him!

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:33.200
I knew it.

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:37.230
That gun... the man who killed 
my father carried the same model.

00:17:38.900 --> 00:17:41.760
You're a Grandiga soldier, aren't you?

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:44.550
Be extra careful, okay?

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:46.750
I am, chill out.

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:56.130
Watch it!

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:57.590
Are you people nuts?!

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:07.560
Good job, Pierce.

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:09.310
Much obliged.

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:14.720
Commander, we have the new chrars 
and we've set the explosives.

00:18:14.720 --> 00:18:16.200
How are things with you?

00:18:16.600 --> 00:18:19.960
I'm in front of the administrative
 building. I'm still on base.

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:21.670
Hey!

00:18:21.670 --> 00:18:23.450
Keep following the plan!

00:18:24.720 --> 00:18:26.280
I'll say this one more time.

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:30.210
When the plant underground blows up, 
it'll kill everyone here.

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:32.090
So don't blow it up.

00:18:32.410 --> 00:18:33.340
I can't do that.

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:38.060
What are you doing?

00:18:38.360 --> 00:18:39.340
Get in the truck!

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:41.850
Cancel the detonation!

00:18:47.910 --> 00:18:50.650
Each time you refuse, I'll kill one of them.

00:18:55.920 --> 00:18:57.900
Miss...

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:01.350
You...

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:05.580
They're dead either way, 
so what does it matter?

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:21.970
Hey, it's time to split!

00:19:44.590 --> 00:19:47.560
The Royal Army will be here soon.

00:19:47.560 --> 00:19:49.000
Keep them safe.

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:51.330
Don't expect us to thank you.

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:53.230
I hope you all die!

00:19:53.230 --> 00:19:55.000
Murderers! Leave us alone!

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:56.410
Murderers!

00:19:56.410 --> 00:19:57.610
Get away from us!

00:19:57.610 --> 00:19:59.100
Murderers!

00:19:59.100 --> 00:20:00.760
Go away!

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:02.890
Murderers!

00:20:02.890 --> 00:20:04.010
Mama...

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:08.110
Lana.

00:20:08.110 --> 00:20:09.520
I'm sorry about—

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:18.530
Give back my papa and mama.

00:20:19.120 --> 00:20:22.530
My home... everything...

00:20:25.220 --> 00:20:26.110
Let's go.

00:20:38.190 --> 00:20:41.300
This is the nature of what we're doing.

00:20:41.570 --> 00:20:45.540
Yet you're certain you can fight on, 
for as long as it takes?

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:56.990
You did an excellent job.

00:20:56.990 --> 00:20:59.910
We were having a little talk, just now...

00:21:00.390 --> 00:21:05.790
What if someone had died while 
you were AWOL during the mission?

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:09.780
It's a commander's job to 
trust his subordinates.

00:21:10.280 --> 00:21:12.200
Oh, clever.

00:21:13.170 --> 00:21:14.540
Where's Stella?

00:21:15.860 --> 00:21:18.500
I'm afraid I don't know.

00:21:34.630 --> 00:21:37.350
Looks like it got to you more than expected.

00:21:37.680 --> 00:21:38.810
What do you mean?

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:41.610
If you mean the all-nighter, 
I'm used to night missions.

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:46.610
I wonder when our next mission will be.

00:21:50.650 --> 00:21:52.490
<i>She's gone mad.</i>

00:23:35.100 --> 00:23:40.480
<b><i>Choice of Hope</i></b>
